# patches_lossy_gate_expanded_corpus_2026-05-17.tsv

## Provenance
- Issue #45 (patches gate expanded corpus calibration).
- Re-runs RFC#45 chunks 4-7's lossy `is_cost_effective` calibration
  shape on an expanded screenshot corpus (25 instead of 5) + 15-photo
  no-regression panel to test whether the larger corpus shifts the
  fit of `SAVINGS_BYTES_PER_PIXEL` (chunk 4/5), the 1/sqrt(d_clamped)
  divisor (chunk 5), or the 1.5× safety margin (chunk 6).

## Generation
```
cd jxl-encoder--patches-expanded-corpus
cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder \
  --example patches_lossy_gate_expanded_corpus \
  --features __internals \
  > benchmarks/patches_lossy_gate_expanded_corpus_2026-05-17.tsv
```

## Environment
- Parent commit (main@origin): 336829f135f6fff69781b51c54739d742678383e
  (`perf(modular/patches): lossless-shape trial encoder + tighter C
  (RFC#45 lossless chunk 5)`)
- Hostname: lilith (water-cooled Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM)
- Date: 2026-05-17 (UTC)
- jxl-encoder version: 0.3.2

## Grid
- 11 gb82-sc + 14 qoi-benchmark/screenshot_web = 25 screenshots
- 5 CID22-512 + 5 clic2025-1024 + 5 gb82-photos = 15 photos
- 4 distances: {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0}
- 40 images × 4 distances = 160 measured cells
- `LossyConfig::new(d).with_mode(EncoderMode::Experimental)` —
  Experimental is the mode where the per-set `is_cost_effective` gate
  is the ONLY patches gate (Reference mode admits patches and runs
  the per-patch gate so the per-set constant is invisible there).
- patches-on = default; patches-off = `with_patches(false)` sidecar.
- `LastPatchesStats` thread-local snapshot captures detection stats
  *after* per-patch gating (the only path with the per-set gate
  visible).

## Schema
class                 screenshot|photo
image                 file basename
width / height        pixels
distance              {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0}
bytes_off             bytes with patches=false
bytes_on              bytes with patches=default
actual_savings_B      bytes_off - bytes_on (signed)
total_patch_pixels    sum over occurrences of ref.xsize * ref.ysize
unique_refs           PatchesData::ref_positions.len() AFTER per-patch gate
ref_frame_pixels      ref_width * ref_height AFTER per-patch gate
occurrences           PatchesData::positions.len() AFTER per-patch gate
empirical_bpp_sqrt_d  actual_savings_B * sqrt(max(d,1.0)) / total_patch_pixels
                      (the chunk-5 fit shape: 0.78 is the geomean over the
                      original 5-screenshot × 4-distance grid)

## Notes
- `bytes_on == bytes_off` with `total_patch_pixels > 0` indicates the
  gate REJECTED the detection (matches our calibration's intent — the
  per-image cost outweighs estimated savings).
- For C-fit: gather all rows with `total_patch_pixels > 0 AND
  actual_savings_B > 0` (gate admitted AND empirically won), then
  `geomean(empirical_bpp_sqrt_d)` ≈ chunk-5's 0.78 — verify if expanded
  corpus shifts this.
- For C-rejection floor: gather all rows with `actual_savings_B < 0`
  (gate admitted but lost bytes) — currently expected to be empty
  (gate is conservative); if non-empty, C is too low.

## Per-cell c_needed (post-process)
For a given C, the per-cell admission verdict is:
  `total_patch_pixels * C / sqrt(max(d,1.0)) * 2 >= 3 * total_overhead`
where `total_overhead` is derived from the lossless calibration TSV
(same image, same detection — overhead is distance-invariant since
patches detection runs on pre-gaborish XYB).

## Verdict (2026-05-17)

**No constant change required. Current `SAVINGS_BYTES_PER_PIXEL = 0.78`
holds on expanded corpus.**

### Headline numbers
- 25 screenshots × 4 distances = 100 cells, 1 OOM (phoboslab @ d=4.0)
  → 99 measured cells.
- 15 photos × 4 distances = 60 cells, all encoded.
- Detected: 87 / 99 screenshot cells, 0 / 60 photo cells.
- Admitted (won bytes): 58 / 87 detected cells.
- Rejected (gate said no, savings=0): 29 / 87 detected cells.
- **Zero regressions** (no admitted cell loses bytes).
- **Total screenshot savings: 13.07 MB (26.0% of bytes_off)**.
- **Photo bytes byte-identical 60/60 cells, 0 detections, 0 overhead.**

### Empirical bpp_sqrt_d distribution on admitted (n=58)
- min:     0.2329
- p10:     0.4883
- p25:     0.6722
- median:  0.8041
- geomean: **0.8005** (current C=0.78; within 3% of fit target)
- mean:    0.8575
- max:     1.8212

### Per-distance geomean of empirical_bpp_sqrt_d
- d=0.50: n=16, geomean=0.8848
- d=1.00: n=16, geomean=0.7805
- d=2.00: n=14, geomean=0.7943
- d=4.00: n=12, geomean=0.7313

All four distances are within 10% of C=0.78. The `1/sqrt(d_clamped)`
shape is robust on the expanded corpus.

### 1.5× safety margin
26 of 58 admitted cells have `empirical_bpp_sqrt_d < C = 0.78` — they
would be FALSE-NEGATIVE-rejected by a strict C-only model, but win
bytes thanks to the 1.5× margin (the gate admits when est-savings is
only ⅔ of overhead, so ⅔ × C = 0.52 is the effective floor). All 26
empirically WIN bytes → margin is correctly tuned.

### New finds vs original 5-screenshot fit
The expanded corpus surfaces winning cells in:
- `news.ycombinator.com.png` (4/4 d, 41-86 KB savings each)
- `nytimes.com.png` (4/4 d, 47-194 KB savings)
- `reddit.com.png` (2/4 d at low-d, 67-79 KB savings)
- `phoboslab.org.png` (3/4 d, 846 KB-1.2 MB savings — biggest absolute win)
- All gb82-sc admissions hold.

Total bytes added by expanded corpus: ~5.7 MB additional savings.

### Decision
- **NO change to `SAVINGS_BYTES_PER_PIXEL = 0.78`.**
- **NO change to `1/sqrt(d_clamped)` divisor shape.**
- **NO change to 1.5× safety margin.**
- Calibration is robust on 5× larger screenshot corpus + 3× larger photo set.
